# Project docs (humans and agents)

Before non-trivial work in this repo:

1. Open [`docs/README.md`](docs/README.md) and pick the matching **concern** doc (data, billing, authentication-and-authorization, conventions, …).
2. Prefer official docs for the versions in `package.json` (Next: also `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` — see `AGENTS.md`).
3. **Concern over vendor** — durable docs are named for the concern; Stripe/Clerk/Query live *inside* those pages.
4. **One tool per job** — choose carefully; once adopted, don’t invent a parallel stack for the same purpose (second billing provider, second auth system, SWR beside Query, Lodash beside es-toolkit, Jest beside Vitest, Cypress beside Playwright, …). **Replace** only if the other tool can do everything (or nearly everything) the current one does, better — and document it in the concern doc. See [`docs/conventions.md`](docs/conventions.md) · [`docs/vocabulary.md`](docs/vocabulary.md).
5. Code comments and rules should point at a **file** (e.g. `docs/billing.md`), not at another doc’s section titles.

Topic-specific rules (e.g. billing) still apply when their globs match; they do not replace this index.
